 "answer": "The function is **`load_index_from_storage`**, imported from `llama_index.core`. You pass it a `StorageContext`, which you typically create with `StorageContext.from_defaults(persist_dir=...)`:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.core import StorageContext, load_index_from_storage\n\nstorage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(persist_dir=\"./storage\")\nindex = load_index_from_storage(storage_context)\n```\n\nIf the storage directory holds more than one index, pass `index_id` to pick one. To save an index, call `index.storage_context.persist(persist_dir=\"./storage\")`.",
